 "result_text": "I fixed the intermittent `test_add_dataset` failure; I didn't look into the `test_round_trip` one.\n\n**Cause:** your guess was right. `generate_uid()` appended a random number drawn from `[0, 10**n)`. Roughly one draw in ten has fewer than `n` digits, so the UID came out shorter than 64 characters. That shifted the encoded dataset length, which is why the test saw 396 instead of 398.\n\n**Fix:** in `src/pydicom/uid.py`, the random suffix is now always exactly `64 - len(prefix)` digits with no leading zero. Every UID generated without `entropy_srcs` is therefore exactly 64 characters.\n\n**Check:** 20,000 calls to `generate_uid()` all returned 64-character UIDs, and a call with a different prefix (`'1.2.3.'`) also gave 64. I didn't run the test suite, and I didn't change any tests.\n\n**Other test:** I didn't investigate `tests/test_encoders.py::TestDatasetCompress::test_round_trip` (the \"memory re-use\" one). This change shouldn't affect it.",
